---
title: Turkey Gravy
course: sauce
cuisine: american
servings: 10
time_active: 20
time_total: 20
leftovers: good
tags: [holiday]
description: Pan gravy from turkey drippings and store-bought stock.
---

While the turkey roasts, you can simmer the reserved neck and giblets (not the liver) in @chicken stock{4%cups}(low-sodium) ~{30-60%minutes} for more flavor, then strain. Otherwise just warm the stock.

Pour the pan drippings through a #fat separator{} or into a bowl and skim off the fat, saving it.

In a #saucepan{} over medium heat, melt 1/4 cup of the saved fat, topping up with @butter{2%tbsp} if there isn't enough. Whisk in @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup} and cook, whisking, until golden and nutty, ~{2-3%minutes}.

Slowly whisk in the warm stock and the skimmed drippings. Simmer, whisking often, until thick enough to coat a spoon, ~{5-10%minutes}.

Taste before seasoning; the drippings are salty from the brine. Add @black pepper{}, a splash of @?apple cider{1%tbsp} to brighten, and @salt only if it needs it.
